{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaT9nVwpe8p5Rss6uCLF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017chvwwTTs9jNXayDzNcJTc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"{ cat <<'EOF'\n// Hunt for counterexamples to the definite move (loop0006 item 08, paper2/search_soundness.md §4.2).\n//\n// Reads graphs from stdin, one per line: `n m_0 ... m_{n-1}` (self-inclusive neighbourhood\n// masks, n <= 24). For every k, every free-closed state S with |O(S) - S| <= k and a\n// solution, and every playable q not in S whose premise fires, checks that the child\n// cl(S + q) still has a solution; prints `BAD ...` otherwise. MODE selects the premise:\n//   MODE=0 (default)  the code's: open(q, S) <= close(q, S)       -> finds the counterexamples\n//   MODE=1            the repair: hereditary, b(X) <= b(S + E)    -> should print no BAD\n//   MODE=2            the repair's matching form                  -> should print no BAD\n// With any argument, only the first firing q in index order is checked (the code's choice).\n//\n//   gcc -O2 -o /tmp/definite_hunt paper2/definite_hunt.c\n//   python3 paper2/definite_hunt_gen.py 1 3000 10 16 | /tmp/definite_hunt\n//\n// The counterexamples of DEFINITE_CEX in paper2/search_check.py came from family 4 of the\n// generator (the gadget) at 14-16 customers, after 90,000 graphs of the other families at\n// 10-16 gave two; they were minimised by deleting vertices and edges while a BAD remained.\nEOF\nsed -e 's/^typedef uint32_t u32;/typedef uint32_t u32;/' /tmp/dm/thm2.c; } > paper2/definite_hunt.c && { cat <<'EOF'\n\"\"\"Random graphs for `paper2/definite_hunt.c` (loop0006 item 08).\n\n    python3 paper2/definite_hunt_gen.py SEED COUNT NMIN NMAX [FAMILY]\n\nFamilies: 0 G(n, p); 1 tree plus extra edges; 2 bounded degree; 3 union of small cliques\n(MOSP-like); 4 the gadget -- a closed customer s whose open neighbours d_1..d_r share one new\nstack y with q, q's other new stacks z_1..z_t hanging into a random rest. Family 4 is where\nthe definite move's counterexamples live. Default: a family drawn per graph.\n\"\"\"\nEOF\nsed -e 's/n=rng.randint(lo,hi); fam=rng.randrange(5); E=set()/n=rng.randint(lo,hi); fam=int(sys.argv[5]) if len(sys.argv)>5 else rng.randrange(5); E=set()/' /tmp/dm/gen.py; } > paper2/definite_hunt_gen.py && gcc -O2 -o /tmp/dm/hunt paper2/definite_hunt.c 2>&1 | grep -c error; python3 paper2/definite_hunt_gen.py 101 3000 11 16 4 | /tmp/dm/hunt 1 | tail -2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":250413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":606,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39ac369b-d492-4a17-b894-f8de828cd9c3","uuid":"7180768d-1a6c-4a9a-80a2-96ff8a240146","timestamp":"2026-09-30T22:58:09.155Z","request_id":"req_011CfaT9n4ueApmqJvGmaQAr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017chvwwTTs9jNXayDzNcJTc":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && { cat <<'EOF'\n// Hunt for counterexamples to the definite move (loop0006 item 08, paper2/search_soundness.md §4.2).\n//\n// Reads graphs from stdin, one per line: `n m_0 ... m_{n-1}` (self-inclusive neighbourhood\n// masks, n <= 24). For every k, every free-closed state S with |O(S) - S| <= k and a\n// solution, and every playable q not in S whose premise fires, checks that the child\n// cl(S + q) still has a solution; prints `BAD ...` otherwise. MODE selects the premise:\n//   MODE=0 (default)  the code's: open(q, S) <= close(q, S)       -> finds the counterexamples\n//   MODE=1            the repair: hereditary, b(X) <= b(S + E)    -> should print no BAD\n//   MODE=2            the repair's matching form                  -> should print no BAD\n// With any argument, o